--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ six at run time: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
could not be evaluated
static assertion failed
--
The guard against runaway template recursion counted an enclosing instance
of the same template whenever one argument contained the other's spelling,
also when the argument was the same (Len above), and cut the recursion
after three levels: F<L<...5 types...>, 0>::value was not known.  An
unchanged argument is no longer evidence of growth.
